# Append-only board rows and notes. Every feature branch adds a row to the same table tail
# or the same prepend point, so two parallel branches collide on lines neither one got
# wrong. Union keeps both sides. Without this file the collision surfaced as a stash-pop
# conflict on _meta/BACKLOG.md that a session hand-resolved four times in one sitting.
#
# Caveat: union never drops a line, so a single row both sides EDITED comes out duplicated
# rather than merged. `bash lib/board/backlog.sh dedupe-all <file>` clears that, and
# lib/wrap/wrap.sh runs it after a union re-merge. Do not add a whole-document table whose
# rows get rewritten in place.
_meta/BACKLOG.md merge=union
_meta/backlog-staging.md merge=union
docs/implementation-notes/*.md merge=union
